{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back","id":1097316,"title":"Bringing the Fog of Eternity Back","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T15:11:02-07:00","id":1097316,"title":"Bringing the Fog of Eternity Back","content":"so I've thought about the subject a lot- and by &quot;a lot&quot;, I mean since the 2e core has came out- and I've finally came to the conclusion: while I love almost everything about the new edition, I miss the Fog of Eternity. Yeah yeah, I know, &quot;senile elders&quot; and &quot;vampires don't need to lose their minds to avoid having a known origin- they can just lie&quot;, but I really liked that aspect of the game. I mean, it made torpor <i>terrifying</i>. You were afraid from getting staked or starved not only because it made you helpless, but because it threatened to devour your mind. Sleep, which is meant to be something relaxing, turned into something dark and terrible. Vampires have invested their efforts to escape that sleep, or try to preserve their memories. The ideal of &quot;perfected vampire&quot; wasn't a blood-god as much as a vampire which actually remembered everything about their life and death. It added another level of personal horror, another level of detachment from humanity. Vampires, which are usually defined by being static and immune to the passage of time, turned into something which feared time- or at least, the madness it carried. They couldn't even trust their own memories- for who knows what truly happened and what was a product of their own nightmares? Searching for why and how the Fog works and how to protect against it was even the goal of number of few bloodlines and plot hooks. In sort, yeah, it was a big deal in the 1E setting, and I really think it was cool.<br /> <br /> so in sort- how much adaptation do you think would be required to adapt the Fog to 2E in a way which works in the new setting material and mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:26:56-07:00","id":1097322,"title":"","content":"I think it's a trivial change. Very few NPCs and rules rely on fully accurate knowledge of the past, and the precedent for it occurring is already in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:31:39-07:00","id":1097326,"title":"","content":"I was going to say, I think the Fog of Eternity is still a thing in 2nd Edition. I believe the core book just didn't go into it much just like Bloodlines didn't get much except a passing description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T18:00:59-07:00","id":1097377,"title":"","content":"It's described as something that only happens rarely, as an exception to the rule. Instead of the rule like it was in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T08:11:21-07:00","id":1097524,"title":"","content":"Yeah, almost litterally no adjustment needs to be made. There was no ruleset for the fog of ages in 1E (unless I missed some obscure supplement), and the only things that really touched the subject were a few bloodlines. 2E doesn't mention it so it's not really a thing, but yeah, just say it's a thing and you're all set. Go fish for the bloodlines to adapt to 2E if you want, as they're perfectly functional. Theorically, they's supposed to work a little differently, and have a &quot;boon&quot; or something, but the way they worked in 1E can be translated to 2E without any mechanical change for the most part.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the fog not existing would probably change some things in the politics of the cities that have a good chance of having one or more elders swimming around, but as far as I've read, 2E wasn't written to feature super elders as a common thing, so the feel is very similar to 2E. The upcoming book on elders will be, to my knowledge, the first big step towards exploring that in Requiem. Well, ok, there was Zagreus, but he's just one NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:08:49-07:00","id":1097545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1097524#post1097524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, almost litterally no adjustment needs to be made. There was no ruleset for the fog of ages in 1E (unless I missed some obscure supplement), and the only things that really touched the subject were a few bloodlines</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, The Blood has given mechanics for the influence of torpor upon Kindred minds- but yeah, it doesn't look like it would be too complicated to translate them to 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T14:44:23-07:00","id":1097623,"title":"","content":"I never really liked the Fog of Eternity concept, to be honest. Now, it's not that I don't believe that vampires should be these static creatures that remember everything, but I don't think there needs to be any mechanic or special thing behind it. People forget things, so why wouldn't vampires forget things? I figured the reason that vampires have no origin in 2e is that people didn't write that stuff down, and anyone who has been around since then would have most likely forgotten. I just felt like the Fog of Eternity was trying to make something special out of something completely mundane; of course things are going to be fuzzy after 200 years in torpor, you've been having feverish nightmares for the past 200 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T17:48:22-07:00","id":1097644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1097623#post1097623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really liked the Fog of Eternity concept, to be honest. Now, it's not that I don't believe that vampires should be these static creatures that remember everything, but I don't think there needs to be any mechanic or special thing behind it. People forget things, so why wouldn't vampires forget things? I figured the reason that vampires have no origin in 2e is that people didn't write that stuff down, and anyone who has been around since then would have most likely forgotten. I just felt like the Fog of Eternity was trying to make something special out of something completely mundane; of course things are going to be fuzzy after 200 years in torpor, you've been having feverish nightmares for the past 200 years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of this. Look, it can be hard to imagine a time before the photograph and easy communication by post, phone or internet, but it was actually hard to recognize people and there are stories in various epics of best friends falling into duels and the like because they didn't realize each other. That's with a relatively few decades difference. <br /> <br /> The human mind is horrible at remembering details. Honest. Eyewitness testimony is exceptionally flawed and subject to after-the-fact distortion by questioning, other input and the like. Emotional state has a huge bearing on how you remember things, as well. It's not a stretch to expect Kindred to end up gaslighting themselves as they struggle with their beast, and just forget little details like that time they were in Rome with Nero. Eventually, they could forget they were ever in Rome. Unless the vamp has prepared well--very well--their nights are going to be an interminable succession of feeding pressures, challenges, and near-death experiences. That's the Fog of Ages right there, and the horror is nothing has to be invented to make time their enemy.<br /> <br /> Kindred are timeless. Their minds are not. Writing stuff down bites you.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:27:28-07:00","id":1097745,"title":"","content":"*shruggs*<br /> <br /> I am well aware of this, and that most people dislike the Fog as a &quot;thing&quot;- and its ok. Everyone have their own preferences about the game they play. I also know that the vast majority of people support that opinion (after all, I find it hard to believe that 2E would have removed/reduced the Fog is it was the most popular aspect of the game, right?). I, however, think that the Fog of Ages gave the game a certain flavor I really liked. Like I've said in the opening post, it is something I've thought about since 2E has just came out. It is not that I think that without the Fog (as a rule, not the exception) the game is &quot;RUINED FOREVER&quot;- 2E is awesome, and I really enjoy it. I just also miss the Fog- not as just a concept, but as something with teeth, which can bite you down. Be it mundane effect or a supernatural one (after all, getting shot by a gun is also a mundane effect- it still has mechanics), without mechanics the core assumption is that unless the player has decided that their character forgot something during torpor, everything they remember is, more or less, how things happened. <br /> <br /> In sort, I like the concept of the Fog as something which actively devours the minds of sleeping Kindred. I know that most people don't agree with me, and so I don't try to convince anyone that the Fog of Ages should be a thing, but for advice about how to add it to the 2E setting and which modification may be required. Vampire is a great game, with or without the Fog- but until Onyx Path would Kickstart their Edition Ninjas Project in order to force everyone to &quot;play the game the right way&quot;, I'll probably still like the Fog as a &quot;rule and not exception&quot; and think about adding it to my games and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:10:19-07:00","id":1097905,"title":"","content":"Well, there might be some stuff in Thousand Years of Night when it comes to Kindred forgetting things, so we'll have to check that out. However, in regards for getting shot having mechanics that's probably because that's more likely to occur in the game than long periods of torpor.<br /> <br /> However, you asked about mechanics. I believe that the whole mind devouring thing should be reasonable; if you're in torpor for a week, you forget mostly minor things. However, the longer that time in torpor is the more effect the Fog of Eternity should have. It'd also be prudent to have it coincide with your level of humanity; with low humanity you're more bestial and instinctual, so it should hit you harder. However, with high humanity you aren't so ruled by your base urges, so the blow should be softened, somewhat. When it comes to rolling I'd make it an resolve+composure roll limited by their humanity; they're trying to keep their memories from being wrested from them.<br /> <br /> However, I think the fog of eternity concept might be hard to put into a game because you can't make the players forget things, and some of them will slip up and say something that their character shouldn't know anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T01:17:35-07:00","id":1098017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1097905#post1097905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, I think the fog of eternity concept might be hard to put into a game because you can't make the players forget things, and some of them will slip up and say something that their character shouldn't know anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, that is a role playing game- if the player forgets their character forgot, it is the ST job to notice and correct them. And If both of them didn't notice, than it shouldn't be a problem, right? :P<br /> <br /> And yeah, those mechanics seem to be pretty much what we have at the Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:15:58-07:00","id":1098045,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea, more or less inspired from the atrocity dice thing or the paradox from mage. Let's say sleeps for a given number of years. How about for each set number of years (every year, every five year, every decade...), they earn some kind of &quot;torpor point&quot;. Then, whenever they make a mental roll to recall something, be it remembering a certain fact or a certain type of knowledge (Science, Academics, Politics) that they learned about before they went into torpor, the GM can decide, if it's appropriate, to make the character use up one (or more) of those torpor dice. Maybe they have to roll it themselves with their dice pool, or the GM rolls it behind the screen.<br /> <br /> A success on the die is fine and changes nothing, a failure removes one success, a 1 adds gives a misleading result to the roll (ex : How do you make gunpowder, Roll intelligence + science or academics, torpor die ends up 1, &quot;Well, gunpowder explodes, so you should add something spicy like pepper&quot;) and 10 gives an additional knowledge the character didn't learn back then, but was granted to him via some torpor induced insight (it could also effectively change their memory so they remember learning about it, but the information is real or at least helpful).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:28:18-07:00","id":1098317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1098017#post1098017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And yeah, those mechanics seem to be pretty much what we have at the Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I've never read the Blood, or heard of it for that matter. Might be an interesting book to pick up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T01:55:22-07:00","id":1098378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1098317#post1098317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I've never read the Blood, or heard of it for that matter. Might be an interesting book to pick up.</div> </div> </div> </div>it is the 1E's Player's Handbook- so while it is a really good book, it may be useless/outdated in the new edition- so you should take that into account","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:15:05-07:00","id":1101029,"title":"","content":"If you need a mechanic, memory loss sounds like a derangement to me.<br /> <br /> Maybe one of the functions of torpor in your game could be to clean out the old detritus of derangements that have been accumulating. When vampires experience a full torpor, of a length appropriate to their Humanity, they may trade out another, more troublesome derangement for the loss of memory of a period equal to the length of their torpor. Just describe the derangement as being functionally identical to the Amnesia Condition.<br /> <br /> There could be two forms of the derangement: Repressed Memories (mild), which clouds the memories, but allows the sufferer to spend an XP to ask the ST a single Yes/No question about the period lost, and thereby slowly rebuild the memories; and Infantile Amnesia (severe), in which the memories are gone. Period.<br /> <br /> Whether it is Mild or Severe could depend on whether the derangement it replaces is Mild or Severe.<br /> <br /> Ex 1: A Humanity 4 vampire entered torpor for one year, they could trade out, say, Schizophrenia (severe) for Infantile Amnesia (severe), removing the memories of the one year period in which schizophrenia was originally acquired. The memories are simply gone, and this derangement cannot be removed... though certain disciplines might bend this rule. Go ask the Agonistes, maybe?<br /> <br /> Ex 2: A Humanity 3 vampire entered torpor for five years. They suffer from Suspicion (mild), and choose to trade that out for Repressed Memories (mild), which cloaks the memory of the five year period in which he gained Suspicion. They later need to know if they were in France during that period. They spend an XP to piece together the scattershot images they still have and ask, &quot;Was I in France during that period?&quot; The ST will answer accurately.<br /> <br /> This would make the Fog positively correlated with low Humanity and an unstable mental state. It would also tend to remove the most notable periods of the amnesiac's life, when derangements are mostly likely to be acquired. Plus, torpor is supposed to be filled with dreams and nightmares that recombine elements from memory to re-interpret events. That sounds believably therapeutic enough to allow such a trade.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T00:13:16-07:00","id":1101133,"title":"","content":"That sounds right for 1st ed. but in 2nd there's not such thing as Derragements or Mild/Severe separation of Conditions. <br /> <br /> The idea is very good besides that.<br /> <br /> You could use the False Memories and Amnesia Conditions instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T17:55:57-07:00","id":1103341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1101133#post1101133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds right for 1st ed. but in 2nd there's not such thing as Derragements or Mild/Severe separation of Conditions.<br /> <br /> The idea is very good besides that.<br /> <br /> You could use the False Memories and Amnesia Conditions instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are different degrees of Tilts, though, so some manner of severity exists in the rules. Applying that to new Conditions isn't that much of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T09:26:31-07:00","id":1103526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1097905#post1097905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think the fog of eternity concept might be hard to put into a game because you can't make the players forget things, and some of them will slip up and say something that their character shouldn't know anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097316-bringing-the-fog-of-eternity-back?p=1101029#post1101029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need a mechanic, memory loss sounds like a derangement to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We already have the False Memory and Amnesia Conditions, which take care of both these issues, one is rewarding players with beats for playing the Condition to their character's detriment (Be led by false memories to trust someone or take a risk) or (A problem from your lost period emerges) for a more interesting story and are solid existing mechanics.<br /> <br /> The trick would be the guideline to when gaining those conditions would be applicable which is simple to implement, thematically correct, and encourages gameplay which is desired. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> I think a Breaking Points specific to periods spent in torpor, with False Memory for normal Failure, and Amnesia being for Dramatic Failure might be a good start.<br /> <br /> In fact if I was going with the renewal affect of Torpor theme I would have decade periods be the Breaking point threshold for check but have gaining Humanity with getting the Conditions as they fail or dramatically fail their breaking points, as the monsters forget or distort their past of how horrible they are, thus making Torpor like the description of Elders awakening with once again flexible minds as per the current book. And that has the side affect of making these newly humane vampires also extremely inaccurate about their past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-14-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}